  "settingsTelemetrySubtitle": "Counts which features get used — never document content, amounts or text",
  "settingsTelemetryNoticeTitle": "About usage statistics",
  "settingsTelemetryNoticeBody": "To learn what SmartSpend is actually useful for, we count how many times you use each feature, per day — for example \"4 scans started today, 3 saved\".\n\nWhat is sent: the event's name (e.g. scan_started, scan_approved), a categorical choice where the event has one (e.g. your company type), the day, and that day's count. These counters are linked to your account. Plus a random install number generated when you install the app — it exists so that using one account on two devices does not make the counts overwrite each other. It is not your device's hardware identifier: it changes if you reinstall, and is regenerated when you sign out.\n\nHow it is collected: automatically, while you use the app; you are never asked for anything extra.\n\nWhat is never sent: receipt or invoice images, the text read from them, store names, amounts, your notes, your location, and the times of individual actions. Counters are kept per day, so no timeline of what you did and when can be reconstructed.\n\nWhere it goes: we use no third-party analytics service. The data goes to Supabase, the infrastructure provider that hosts all of SmartSpend's data, on servers located abroad. Your data is not used for advertising and is not sold. Details of the international transfer are in the Privacy Policy.\n\nLegal basis: KVKK art. 5/2-f — legitimate interest. We do not ask for explicit consent; instead you can switch this off from this screen in one tap, and nothing in the app is restricted when you do.\n\nSwitching it off stops collection entirely, deletes any counters not yet sent from your device, and requests deletion of the counters already sent from the server. This setting applies to this device only. Deleting your account deletes these counters too.\n\nData controller: İsmail Tunç Kankılıç (SmartSpend). Contact: ismail.tunc.kankilic@gmail.com\n\nHow long it is kept: counters linked to your account are kept for at most 90 days. After that they are turned into statistics that carry no identity, and the record linked to your account is deleted. Statistics coming from too few users to be anonymous are not kept at all — they are deleted rather than aggregated.\n\nYour rights: under KVKK you may learn whether your personal data is being processed, request information about it, ask for it to be corrected, erased or destroyed, and object to the processing. Reach us at the address above; you may also complain to the Turkish Data Protection Authority. Details are in the Privacy Policy.",
